[247.1596, "o", "for p in ['/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base/config.json','/app/merged_model/config.json']:\r\n    c=json.load(open(p))\r\n    c['num_labels']=20\r\n    c['problem_type']='single_label_classification'\r\n    json.dump(c, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\r\n    print(p, 'num_labels now', json.load(open(p))['num_labels'])\r\nEOF — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 - <<'EOF' import json for p in ['/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 17 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 - <<'EOF'\r\nimport torch\r\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForSequenceClassification, AutoTokenizer\r\nm = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(\"/app/merged_model\")\r\nt = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"/app/merged_model\")\r\nenc = t(\"Hello, how are you?\", return_tensors=\"pt\")\r\nwith torch.no_grad():\r\n    lg = m(**enc).logits[0]\r\nprint(\"num_labels:\", m.config.num_labels, \"| argmax:\", int(lg.argmax()), \"| conf:\", round(float(torch.softmax(lg,-1).max()),4))\r\nEOF — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 - <<'EOF' import tor"]
[247.159726, "o", "ch from transformers import AutoModelForSe…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 18 tool call(s) so far\r\nAll done. Summary:\r\n\r\n**What was set up**\r\n- Installed `torch` (CPU), `transformers`, `peft`, `sentencepiece`, `numpy`.\r\n- Downloaded `FacebookAI/xlm-roberta-base` and `dominguesm/xlm-roberta-base-lora-language-detection` (LoRA r=8, α=16, targets `query`/`value`, with the 20-class `classifier` head in `modules_to_save`).\r\n- `/app/setup_model.py` builds the base as `XLMRobertaForSequenceClassification` with `num_labels=20`, saves it + tokenizer to `/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base`, applies the adapter via `PeftModel.from_pretrained`, then `merge_and_unload()` and saves the merged model to `/app/merged_model/`.\r\n\r\n**Verification**\r\n- Both saved configs report `num_labels: 20`; the merged model reloads cleanly and reproduces the same predictions.\r\n- All 10 test samples classified with high confidence (0.936–0.997), one class per language, written to `/app/detection_results.json` in the requested"]
[247.159746, "o", " format (`text`, `predicted_class_id` from raw argmax of logits, `confidence` = softmax of the winning logit).\r\n\r\n**Notes**\r\n- The adapter's own `config.json` carries the 20-language `id2label` (ar, bg, de, el, en, es, fr, hi, it, ja, nl, pl, pt, ru, sw, th, tr, ur, vi, zh); I used it only to sanity-check the argmax outputs, not to map predictions — the JSON contains only argmax IDs as required.\r\n- One quirk: transformers 5.x dropped `num_labels` from the serialized config, so I wrote it back into both `config.json` files after saving; reloads confirm 20 classes.\r\n- The adapter's reported accuracy on its training set is 99.43%, consistent with the ≥95% target on the hidden set.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.8-27b tools=18 surface=1ff9b2b7005d\r\n"]
